<RCC>
    <qresource prefix="/images">
        <!-- MuiBuilderQt's own program icon - window titlebar (Linux) and
             QApplication-wide default window icon (see main.cpp). The
             Windows .exe icon (taskbar/Explorer/Alt-Tab) is embedded
             separately at link time via RC_ICONS in MuiBuilderQt.pro
             (images/muibuilderqt.ico) - that one is NOT loaded from this
             Qt resource, it's a native Windows resource baked into the
             binary itself. Designed to read as the same visual family as
             AmigaED's own images/amiga_classic.png (matching rainbow
             accent colours sampled from it), but with a shape of its own
             (a small GUI-window mockup) rather than reusing AmigaED's
             checkmark logo for a different application.

             The explicit alias= below is required, not cosmetic: without
             it, rcc keeps the file's path relative to this .qrc (which
             itself lives in gui/, so the on-disk path is images/
             muibuilderqt.png) nested under the prefix as-is, producing
             the resource path :/images/images/muibuilderqt.png - not
             :/images/muibuilderqt.png as main.cpp/mainwindow.cpp
             reference it. That mismatch was actually hit and diagnosed
             here: the earlier alias-less version built and linked
             without any error, but every QIcon(":/images/
             muibuilderqt.png") load silently returned a non-null-but-
             empty icon (0 available sizes) at runtime, so the .exe/app
             build looked fine while the icon simply never appeared
             anywhere. translations.qrc above already gets this right by
             using alias= on its own <file> entries - this mirrors that
             pattern. -->
        <file alias="muibuilderqt.png">images/muibuilderqt.png</file>
    </qresource>
</RCC>
